# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Other Python packages: accepted known vulnerabilities (reviewed 2026-10-29)
#
# Found by the first image scan (build of sha-7d0c751). Fixing these needs a
# major version Forge Neo does not support, or there is no newer release.
# Listed with their impact in README.md, "Known security issues". Same expiry
# rule as above. (GitPython, diffusers and setuptools were upgraded instead.)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# transformers 4.57.6 (Neo pin), fix needs 5.x. Remote code execution when loading a Hub model with remote code.
CVE-2026-4372 exp:2027-01-31
# transformers 4.57.6, fix 5.5.0. trust_remote_code setting can be overridden.
CVE-2026-5241 exp:2027-01-31
# transformers 4.57.6, fix 5.10.0. save_pretrained path traversal via chat template names.
CVE-2026-9856 exp:2027-01-31
# protobuf 4.25.9 (Neo pin), fix needs 5.29.6/6.33.5. Denial of service via deep recursion.
CVE-2026-0994 exp:2027-01-31
# starlette 0.50.0, fix needs 1.x (blocked by FastAPI 0.127 / Gradio 4). Windows-only UNC path SSRF.
CVE-2026-48818 exp:2027-01-31
# starlette 0.50.0, fix 1.3.1. Form size limits ignored for urlencoded forms (DoS).
CVE-2026-54283 exp:2027-01-31
# The next five are copies vendored INSIDE pip 26.2.2 (the newest pip; see pip's
# _vendor/vendor.txt). They only run while pip installs extension packages.
# The image's own urllib3 is >= 2.8.0 (fixed); the Dockerfile asserts that, so
# these entries cannot hide a vulnerable top-level urllib3.
# pip-vendored msgpack 1.1.2, fix 1.2.3. Memory leak DoS during map deserialization.
CVE-2026-114613 exp:2027-01-31
# pip-vendored msgpack 1.1.2, fix 1.2.1. Out-of-bounds read on Unpacker reuse.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 exp:2027-01-31
# pip-vendored urllib3 2.7.0, fix 2.8.0. HTTPS proxy TLS configuration override.
CVE-2026-97687 exp:2027-01-31
# pip-vendored urllib3 2.7.0, fix 2.8.0. Unbounded memory in chunk parser (DoS).
CVE-2026-97689 exp:2027-01-31
# pip-vendored setuptools 70.3.0 (pkg_resources), fix 78.1.1. PackageIndex path traversal.
# The image's own setuptools is 81.0.0 (asserted in the Dockerfile).
CVE-2025-47273 exp:2027-01-31
